.TH "BASH\-SERVER\-CLIENT\-JAVA" "7" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server concepts"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Java client binding provides a blocking, thread\-safe interface to
the bash\-server v2 NDJSON protocol.
It is implemented as the \f[CR]org.gnu.bash:bashclient\f[R] Maven
artifact, requires Java 11 or later, and depends on junixsocket for Unix
domain socket support and Jackson for JSON processing.
.PP
The binding uses a daemon reader thread that continuously reads from the
transport and dispatches messages to per\-channel
\f[CR]BlockingQueue\f[R] instances.
Channel methods block the calling thread (with a 30\-second default
timeout) until the response arrives.
.SH CONCEPTS
.SH Installation
The library is located at \f[CR]bash\-server/clients/java/\f[R] and uses
Maven:
.IP
.EX
cd bash\-server/clients/java
mvn package
.EE
.PP
This produces \f[CR]target/bashclient\-0.1.0.jar\f[R].
.PP
To run tests:
.IP
.EX
mvn test
.EE
.SH Maven coordinates
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]dependency\f[R]>
